3. Allocation per operation (N = 5 000 unless stated)
======================================================================================

  Bytes allocated (JS heap + WASM heap), median of repetitions
  operation                                                allocated  GCs   JS peak ≥
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  write cold N=5000                                        91.92 MiB    2   39.06 MiB
  write cold N=20000                                      367.15 MiB    5  105.95 MiB
  write identical N=5000                                   88.42 MiB    1   71.05 MiB
  write 1-changed N=5000                                   88.41 MiB    1   71.05 MiB
  read cold N=5000                                         95.24 MiB    1   68.89 MiB
  read warm N=5000                                           6.9 KiB    0     6.9 KiB
  read after 1 dirty N=5000                                 7.22 MiB    0    7.22 MiB
  broadcast to 50 watches after a 1-changed write N=5000  134.14 MiB    1   72.49 MiB
  100 single-field writes in one batch, 1 watch, N=5000    15.71 MiB    0   15.71 MiB

  'JS peak ≥' is the highest JS heap seen during the operation above its start,
  sampled at each collection and at the end: a lower bound on the true peak.

======================================================================================
4. Retained by watches, distinct documents and optimistic layers (2 000 entities)
======================================================================================

  Retained bytes, cumulative, and each stage's increment
  stage                                 retained   increment
  ----------------------------------------------------------
  store + read                          9.61 MiB           -
  + 200 watches of one document        18.88 MiB    9.27 MiB
  + 50 watches of distinct documents  214.31 MiB  195.43 MiB
  store + read + 1 watch               18.16 MiB           -
  + 16 optimistic layers               18.39 MiB   240.0 KiB
  after removing the 16 layers         18.37 MiB   -29.7 KiB

  Watches of one document share the memo; each distinct document builds its own
  (performance §4.5), up to the memo's LRU limits.

======================================================================================
5. Steady workloads: memory must plateau, not grow
======================================================================================

  Retained at the end of each workload
  workload                                                                   retained     trend
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  rolling window: 5 live pages of 100, write + read + evict + gc per page   30.91 MiB     GROWS
  watch churn: subscribe + unsubscribe over 1 000 entities                   7.11 MiB  plateaus
  optimistic churn: add + remove a layer over 1 000 entities                 7.02 MiB  plateaus
  document churn: a freshly parsed document per read over 1 000 entities   530.40 MiB     GROWS

  A workload plateaus when its retained memory stops growing: the check projects the
  least-squares slope of the second half over that half, and allows 10 % of the final
  value or 256 KiB. Bounded caches that fill up slowly (Apollo's memo LRUs) can grow
  for longer than the run; the checkpoints in --json show the curve.

